      "player": "Grok4 Stoic",
      "decision_index": 49,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "When resolving Stock Up with 5 Lesson cards in graveyard and Gran-Gran reducing costs, Accumulate Wisdom would cost just {U} and draw 3 cards - arguably the strongest option available. A second Monument to Endurance is decent but less immediately impactful than the massive card advantage Accumulate Wisdom provides in this board state.",
      "action_taken": "Selected Monument to Endurance as one of the two cards from Stock Up",
      "better_line": "Accumulate Wisdom should be a top priority pick - it's essentially Ancestral Recall ({U} draw 3) in this game state with 5+ Lessons in graveyard and Gran-Gran's cost reduction active",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 204,
      "player": "GPT5n Valley",
      "decision_index": 57,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "When ordering cards to the bottom of the library from Stock Up, the player put Island closest to the top instead of Accumulate Wisdom. With 4 Lesson cards already in graveyard, Accumulate Wisdom would draw all 3 cards it looks at (instead of just 1), making it far more valuable than a land drop when the player already has 6 lands and 2 more lands in hand.",
      "action_taken": "Put Island closest to the top of the bottom pile, burying Accumulate Wisdom deeper",
      "better_line": "Put Accumulate Wisdom closest to the top of the bottom pile, as it's the most powerful draw with 3+ Lessons in graveyard, while Island is nearly useless with lands already in hand",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 205,
      "player": "GPT5n Valley",
      "decision_index": 57,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "GPT5n Valley is activating Monument to Endurance during their own end step with all lands tapped. However, Monument to Endurance is a static artifact with triggered abilities (whenever you discard a card, choose one...) - it doesn't have an activated ability. Looking more carefully at the choices, this appears to be casting Monument to Endurance from hand, but all 6 lands are tapped, so there's no mana available to cast it (it costs {3}). Actually, reviewing the board state: Monument to Endurance is already on the battlefield, so this choice must be something else. Wait - looking again at the hand, Monument to Endurance IS in hand, and it's also on the battlefield. That seems like an error in tracking, but taking the decision at face value: they're trying to cast Monument to Endurance for {3} with all lands tapped. This shouldn't be possible. If the game allowed it somehow, the real question is whether this was the right choice among the options. The key issue is that Gran-Gran has 'noncreature spells cost {1} less with 3+ Lessons in graveyard' - there are 6 Lesson cards in the graveyard (Iroh's Demonstration, Firebending Lesson, Abandon Attachments, Accumulate Wisdom, Boomerang Basics, and possibly others). So Monument costs {2} with Gran-Gran's discount. But still, all lands appear tapped. However, Gran-Gran becomes tapped to draw/discard - it's not shown as tapped. Actually the real play here should have been to land a land first (Steam Vents or Multiversal Passage from hand) to have more mana available on future turns, or hold up Spell Snare. Playing Monument to Endurance is reasonable for long-game value with all the discard synergy, but they should have played a land drop first if they hadn't this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Monument to Endurance during end step",
      "better_line": "Should have played a land (Steam Vents or Multiversal Passage) earlier this turn to not miss a land drop and hold up Spell Snare with open mana. Monument to Endurance is fine to cast but sequencing land drops is important.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 220,
      "player": "GPT5n Valley",
      "decision_index": 61,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Monument to Endurance is on the stack and will generate enormous value with Gran-Gran's loot trigger (draw/treasure/3 life loss each turn), plus synergy with the opponent's discard-heavy deck. Three Steps Ahead in counter mode ({1}{U}{U}) was available and affordable with the current mana base (Watery Grave + Undercity Sewers for UU, Swamp/Demolition Field for generic). Failing to counter this must-answer threat allows the opponent to snowball card advantage and damage every turn.",
      "action_taken": "Did not counter Monument to Endurance while it was on the stack",
      "better_line": "Counter Monument to Endurance with Three Steps Ahead (counter mode: {1}{U}{U}) using Watery Grave + Undercity Sewers + Swamp/Demolition Field, preventing the opponent from generating recurring value off discard triggers",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 219,
      "player": "Grok4 Stoic",
      "decision_index": 60,
    }
  ],
